1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Installed as Raja of Kelantan, 1667. Captured by the Siamese and forced to become a concubine of the King of Siam. m. (first) her cousin, Raja 'Abdu'llah bin Sultan Samir ud-din Bahar, Raja of Kelantan-Selatan (Je
2 CONC mbal) (d. at Kota Mahligai, 1671, bur. Padang Halban, Melor), second son of Sultan Samir ud-din bin Jamal ud-din, Raja of Kelantan. m. (second) 1671, Sultan 'Abdu'l Rahim bin Sultan Samir ud-din Bahar, Sultan of Kelantan (d. 1675)
2 CONC , younger brother of her first husband, and son of Sultan Samir ud-din bin Jamal ud-din, Raja of Kelantan. She d. or disappeared at Bukit Merak, after 1671.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Puteri Saadong or Mariam (reigned 1663–1667), was the adopted daughter of Siti Wan Kembang (Che Siti), the legendary Queen of Kelantan. Her full title is Tuan Puteri Saadong binti Raja Loyor, Puteri Vijaya Mala, Raja of Jembal, da
2 CONC ughter of Raja Loyor bin Raja Sakti, Raja of Jembal.
2 CONT
2 CONT Puteri Saadong was brought up in Bukit Marak by Che Siti, after her mother died.[1][2] She succeeded her father as Raja of Jembal in 1663, and was later installed as Raja of Kelantan in 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT Che Siti gave Puteri Saadong's hand in marriage to her cousin, Raja Abdullah bin al-Marhum Sultan Samiruddin, Raja of Kelantan-Selatan (Jembal) when the princess was only 15 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was captured by the Siamese and forced to become a concubine of King Narai of Siam (now Thailand) in order to spare her husband's life. Raja Abdullah vowed to wait for her return and never to remarry. However, after several ye
2 CONC ars Raja Abdullah gave up and remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT When Puteri Saadong returned to Bukit Marak to find Raja Abdullah remarried, a quarrel ensured. It was believed that Puteri Saadong, overwhelmed with rage, killed Raja Abdullah with her hair pin.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the incident, Puteri Saadong left Bukit Marak and subsequently disappeared. Raja Abdullah's tomb can still be seen at Padang Halban, Melor in the district of Bachok, Kelantan.
